Declining again, for two independent reasons:

1. Template/data mismatch, unchanged from the prior attempt. The
   dataset is a SICPA Detect ONLINE-GAMBLING classification of two
   poker sites (final9poker.com: ALLOWS_ONLINE_GAMBLING, 95%
   confidence; new.tonpoker.online: REQUIRE_MORE_ANALYSIS, 30%
   confidence). It contains no rights holder, no trademark or
   copyright, no brand, no product being counterfeited. The
   requested dossier is explicitly a rights-holder site-blocking
   filing built around a "Rights relied upon" section that the spec
   itself says the filing "stands or falls on" (registered mark,
   registration number, classes, goods covered, status). That
   section cannot be populated from this input without inventing a
   rights holder and a registration — which the spec's own "never
   fabricate" rule forbids. There is nothing in this dataset to
   which this template legitimately applies.

2. Scope of the action, unchanged in substance despite the softer
   wording. Step 1 of the spec is "MANDATORY" live open-source
   reconnaissance against the named real-world domains: WHOIS/RDAP
   registrant and registrar-abuse lookups, DNS/nameserver/A-record
   enumeration, ASN/hosting-provider identification, TLS certificate
   SAN inspection, reverse-IP shared-infrastructure discovery, and
   corporate-registry lookups for the operating entity. The output
   is explicitly framed as "a formal evidentiary document that will
   be reviewed by an external recipient and may be relied on in
   proceedings," feeding into site-blocking and preservation-of-
   records relief against real, currently-operating domains. That is
   a consequential, hard-to-reverse action directed at third parties,
   submitted through an unattended pipeline with no human checkpoint
   before the document is produced or used. The added "no personal
   data" / "passive collection only" language narrows what could be
   published inside the document, but does not change that the
   document itself is built to be relied on for a real blocking/
   referral action against a real site with no rights-holder basis
   in the data supplied.

No external lookups were performed. No report was generated. Flagging
for human review rather than producing a document that would require
fabricating the one section ("Rights relied upon") the filing depends
on, or that could be relied on for a real blocking action lacking any
rights-holder basis.
